# Memory between chats

Notes that last between chats live in the operator's personal Cursor store:

`/Users/ic/Library/Application Support/Cursor/AgentStores/cursor_agent_stores/u312431413/files/`

If that folder is not there (for example, in a Cloud Agent), skip this rule.

1. At the start of a task, read `MEMORY.md` in that folder. Open a note only
   when its topic matches the task.
2. A note is what was true on its date. Live code, CI and servers win. If a
   note is wrong, fix the note.
3. At the end of a task, save anything that will still matter next week: a
   decision and why, a command that works, a trap. Follow the format in
   `MEMORY.md`.
4. Never save case data, anything from production, secrets, or chat logs. The
   full list is in `MEMORY.md`.
